-- title:
--   Polar differentials under constant field extension: inclusion
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $F$, $K'$, $F'$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, $F'$ a $K'$-algebra, together with algebra maps $K \to K'$, $F \to F'$ and $K \to F'$ making the relevant towers commute (and $K'$, $F$ acting compatibly on $F'$). Assume $K$ and $K'$ are algebraically closed, that `IsCurveOver K F` and `IsCurveOver K' F'` hold — that is, every nonzero element of $F$ (resp. $F'$) has a degree-zero divisor recording its orders at all places, every place has residue field finite over the base field, and $\Omega[F\,\rlap{/}{\ }K]$ (resp. $\Omega[F'\,\rlap{/}{\ }K']$) is free of rank one over $F$ (resp. $F'$) — and that $F$, $F'$ are of essentially finite type over $K$, $K'$. Assume further: there is $x \in F$ transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite over $K(x)$, and likewise $x \in F'$ transcendental over $K'$ with $F'$ finite over $K'(x)$ (`hfg`, `hfg'`); the $K'$-subfield of $F'$ generated by the image of $F$ is all of $F'$ (`hgen`); and at every place $v$ of $F/K$ and every place $w$ of $F'/K'$ the element $v.dCoord = D_{K}(\pi_v)$, respectively $w.dCoord$, spans the module of differentials over $F$, resp. $F'$ (`hdK`, `hdK'`). Here a place is a valuation subring of $F$, proper, containing the image of $K$ and a principal ideal ring. Let $S$ be a set of places of $F/K$. Then for every $\omega \in \Omega[F\,\rlap{/}{\ }K]$ that is regular off $S$ and has at most a simple pole on $S$ (i.e. for each place $v$, $\omega = f \cdot v.dCoord$ with $f$ in the valuation subring of $v$ when $v \notin S$, and $\omega = f \cdot v.dCoord$ with $\pi_v f$ in that valuation subring when $v \in S$), the image `KaehlerDifferential.map K K' F F' ω` satisfies the same conditions relative to the set of places $w$ of $F'/K'$ whose valuation subring contracts along $F \to F'$ to the valuation subring of some $v \in S$.
--
--   This is the inclusion half of the comparison of spaces of differentials with prescribed simple poles under a constant field extension of algebraically closed base fields: the base-change map sends $\Omega(S)$ into $\Omega(S')$, where $S'$ consists of the places of $F'/K'$ lying over $S$. It is used, together with its companion spanning statement, in [`AlgebraicCurve.map_mem_polarDifferentials_and_mem_span_image_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.map_mem_polarDifferentials_and_mem_span_image_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed) and [`AlgebraicCurve.mem_span_image_polarDifferentials_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.mem_span_image_polarDifferentials_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed).
